1
00:00:01,640 --> 00:00:04,880
The Seven Commandments.

2
00:00:04,880 --> 00:00:05,960
One.

3
00:00:05,960 --> 00:00:10,239
Whatever goes upon two legs is an enemy.

4
00:00:10,239 --> 00:00:11,440
Two.

5
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:17,159
Whatever goes upon four legs or has wings is a friend.

6
00:00:17,159 --> 00:00:18,480
Three.

7
00:00:18,480 --> 00:00:22,079
No animal shall wear clothes.

8
00:00:22,079 --> 00:00:23,398
Four.

9
00:00:23,398 --> 00:00:27,199
No animal shall sleep in a bed.

10
00:00:27,199 --> 00:00:28,639
Five.

11
00:00:28,639 --> 00:00:32,398
No animal shall drink alcohol.

12
00:00:32,398 --> 00:00:33,918
Six.

13
00:00:33,918 --> 00:00:38,840
No animal shall kill any other animal.

14
00:00:38,840 --> 00:00:40,239
Seven.

15
00:00:40,239 --> 00:00:43,079
All animals are equal.

16
00:00:43,079 --> 00:00:48,918
It was very neatly written, and except that friend was written friend, and one

17
00:00:48,918 --> 00:00:55,079
of the s's was the wrong way round, the spelling was correct all the way through.

18
00:00:55,079 --> 00:00:58,480
Snowball read it aloud for the benefit of the others.

19
00:00:58,480 --> 00:01:04,280
All the animals nodded in complete agreement. And the cleverer ones at once

20
00:01:04,280 --> 00:01:07,559
began to learn the commandments by heart.

21
00:01:07,559 --> 00:01:13,199
>> Now, comrades, cried Snowball, throwing down the paintbrush.

22
00:01:13,199 --> 00:01:14,920
To the hayfield!

23
00:01:14,920 --> 00:01:19,800
Let us make it a point of honor to get in the harvest more quickly than Jones

24
00:01:19,800 --> 00:01:21,880
and his men could do.

25
00:01:21,880 --> 00:01:27,199
>> But at this moment, the three cows, who had seemed uneasy for some time past,

26
00:01:27,199 --> 00:01:30,840
set up a loud lowing.

27
00:01:30,840 --> 00:01:39,000
They had not been milked for 24 hours, and their udders were almost bursting.

28
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:43,800
After a little thought, the pigs sent for buckets and milked the cows fairly

29
00:01:43,800 --> 00:01:48,599
successfully, their trotters being well adapted to this task.

30
00:01:48,599 --> 00:01:54,320
Soon, there were five buckets of frothing, creamy milk, at which many of

31
00:01:54,320 --> 00:01:58,280
the animals looked with considerable interest.

32
00:01:58,280 --> 00:02:01,559
>> What is going to happen to all that milk?

33
00:02:01,559 --> 00:02:07,159
Jones used sometimes to mix some of it in our mash, >> said one of the hens.

34
00:02:07,159 --> 00:02:13,679
>> Never mind the milk, comrades, >> cried Napoleon, placing himself in front of the buckets.

35
00:02:13,679 --> 00:02:18,480
>> That will be attended to. The harvest is more important. Comrade Snowball will

36
00:02:18,480 --> 00:02:24,559
lead the way. I shall follow in a few minutes. Forward, comrades. The hay is waiting.

37
00:02:24,559 --> 00:02:29,000
>> So, the animals trooped down to the hayfield to begin the harvest. And when

38
00:02:29,000 --> 00:02:31,000
they came back in the evening, it was
